free period, or continued free access — exact terms will be communicated via
Discord before any change takes effect. Nothing in this section constitutes
a guarantee of any specific benefit.

5. PRIVACY AND DATA
Nexus is offline-first, with one real exception: the built-in update
checker talks to GitHub directly (on by default, no Northbyte Studios
server involved, and you can disable it anytime in Settings) to check for
new releases. It sends nothing about you or your vault and downloads
nothing unless you approve it. Beyond that one feature, Nexus makes zero
network calls — encryption, decryption, and license-key verification all
happen locally on your machine, with no server involved. We collect no
personal data, no telemetry, and no usage analytics through the
application itself. Your files never leave your device. See PRIVACY.md for
what limited information is collected during the manual beta-key issuance
process (outside the application).

